You are given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `target`. Your task is to determine if there exist three distinct elements in `nums` such that their sum is equal to `target`. If such elements exist, return `true`; otherwise, return `false`.

### Input Format
The first line contains an integer `n` (0 ≤ n ≤ 3000) — the length of the array.  
The second line contains `n` space-separated integers representing the elements of `nums`.  
The third line contains a single integer `target` (−10⁵ ≤ target ≤ 10⁵).

### Output Format
Print `true` if there exist three distinct elements whose sum equals `target`, otherwise print `false`.

### Example
**Input**:
```
5
-1 0 1 2 -1
0
```

**Output**:
```
true
```

### Constraints
- The same element cannot be used more than once in each combination.
- The array `nums` can be of any length, including empty.
- Time complexity should be better than O(n³); an efficient solution (e.g., O(n²)) is expected.

### Java 17 Solution
Write a complete Java program that reads the input as described above and outputs `true` or `false` accordingly.

```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static boolean threeSum(int[] nums, int target) {
        Arrays.sort(nums);
        int n = nums.length;
        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {
            if (i > 0 && nums[i] == nums[i - 1]) {
                continue;
            }
            int left = i + 1;
            int right = n - 1;
            while (left < right) {
                int currentSum = nums[i] + nums[left] + nums[right];
                if (currentSum == target) {
                    return true;
                } else if (currentSum < target) {
                    left++;
                } else {
                    right--;
                }
            }
        }
        return false;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = scanner.nextInt();
        int[] nums = new int[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            nums[i] = scanner.nextInt();
        }
        int target = scanner.nextInt();

        boolean result = threeSum(nums, target);
        System.out.println(result);
    }
}
```

